hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2764","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn ‘Umar ibn ‘Ali ibn ‘Ata’ ibn Maqdam al-Muqaddami, who narrated:
On the authority of al-Khalil ibn ‘Uthman, who said: I heard ‘Abdullah ibn Nubayh on the authority of his grandmother Safiyyah bint Shaybah, on the authority of her grandmother Umm Abi Tajz’ah, who said:

""During the pre-Islamic period (Jahiliyyah), we had a small shed (khilfah) between al-Safa and al-Marwah. She said: I looked through a small opening between al-Safa and al-Marwah and saw the Prophet (ﷺ) running (sa’y). He was saying to his companions: 'Run, for Allah has ordained running (sa’y) upon you.'

I saw him running with such intensity that his lower garment (izar) was circling around his waist, so much so that I saw the whiteness of his abdomen and thighs.""

**CHAPTER:**"
"2765","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya, narrated to us 'Abd al-Razzaq, who informed us Ma'mar, on the authority of Wasil, the freed slave of Abu 'Uyaynah, from Musa ibn 'Ubayd, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, that a woman informed her that she had heard the Prophet (ﷺ) between al-Safa and al-Marwah saying: *""It has been prescribed for you to perform the Sa'i (the walk between the two hills), so perform the Sa'i.""*

Abu Bakr (the narrator) said: This is the woman who was not named in this narration—Habibah bint Abi Tajazzah.

**CHAPTER:**"
